# What glibc's installed headers differ by between releases, measured rather than assumed.
#
# One record per line, tab separated, in this order:
#
#   file  first  last  changed at
#
# The file is a path under the installed include directory. First and last are the oldest and the
# newest release in the survey that install it. Changed at is every release whose copy of the file is
# not the code the release before it had, or a dash for a file that has never changed.
#
# Produced by bin/glibc-versions, which is where the method is written down: one install per release
# for the x86_64 ABI, and a comparison of the code in each file rather than of its bytes, because
# glibc bumps a copyright year in every file every January and that is not something a merged tree
# would have to write a conditional for.
